To create a list of random numbers in Java, you can use the `Random` class from the `java.util` package along with an `ArrayList`. Here's a simple example that generates a list of 10 random integers between 0 and 99:

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Random;

public class RandomNumberList {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Random random = new Random();
        List<Integer> randomNumbers = new ArrayList<>();

        // Generate 10 random numbers
        for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
            int randomNumber = random.nextInt(100); // Random number between 0 and 99
            randomNumbers.add(randomNumber);
        }

        // Print the list of random numbers
        System.out.println("List of random numbers: " + randomNumbers);
    }
}
```

